%description:

Tcp.windowScalingFactor:explicit -- a factor from 0 to 14 is the shift count of the SYN.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "Window Scaling Factor given as a shift count. Valid values are 0..14".

The classes: auto (-1, the default), explicit (0 to 14), invalid (below -1 or above 14),
too-small (a factor that cannot represent advertisedWindow). The code:
TcpConnection::configureStateVariables() checks the value, and the options of the SYN select
the factor. This test separates "explicit" from "auto".

Host under test: host1, with advertisedWindow = 262144. Observation: level 1, the Window Scale
option of the SYN of host1 has the shift count 7.

%# parameter: Tcp.windowScalingFactor
%# class: explicit
%# value: 7
%# key: *.host1.tcp.windowScalingFactor
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"
#include "TcpMutations.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpWindowScalingFactorExplicit")
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
                  .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == false")
                  .first()
                  .assertEvent([](const MatchContext& context) { return tcpWindowScaleOptionOf(context.event.packet) == 7; })
                  .describe("the SYN of host1, with the shift count 7")
                  .within(0.5));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpWindowScalingFactorExplicit compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.windowScalingFactor = 7    # the parameter under test
*.host1.tcp.advertisedWindow = 262144
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpWindowScalingFactorExplicit: PASS
